## Hands-on Implementation

The Jupyter Notebook included in this repository demonstrates the practical implementation of Linear Regression using Python.

The implementation covers:

- Importing required Python libraries
- Loading and exploring the dataset
- Data preprocessing and visualization
- Building a Linear Regression model
- Training the model
- Making predictions
- Evaluating model performance
- Visualizing actual and predicted values

## Learning Outcomes

After completing this programme, participants will be able to:

- Explain the concepts and principles of Linear Regression.
- Differentiate between Simple and Multiple Linear Regression.
- Implement regression models using Python.
- Interpret regression coefficients and model predictions.
- Evaluate regression models using appropriate performance metrics.
- Apply regression techniques to real-world predictive analytics problems.

## Target Participants

Faculty members, research scholars, postgraduate students, and academicians interested in Machine Learning, Data Science, and Predictive Analytics.

## Platform

Google Colab – https://colab.research.google.com/

## Conclusion

This FDP provides a combination of theoretical understanding and hands-on experience in Linear Regression, enabling participants to apply predictive modelling techniques in academic, research, and real-world applications.

